# Project Core Principles

- Preserve existing architecture unless the task explicitly authorizes change.
- Inspect relevant code, docs, and Makefile targets before editing.
- Make the smallest safe diff that satisfies the task.
- One task = one responsibility; avoid unrelated cleanup or drive-by refactors.
- No speculative refactors or hidden compatibility breaks.
- Do not silently introduce dependencies, endpoints, or configuration.
- Report unresolved assumptions instead of guessing.
- The repository is the technical source of truth over generic preferences.
- Public contracts remain compatible unless the task explicitly changes them.
- Never commit `.env`, secrets, or credentials.
- Commit and push only when explicitly requested.
